; startup-sequence of the mpdisk boot CD: mount the hardfiles, then hand the
; system over to MPD0: and run its own Startup-sequence (Workbench).
;
; RMTM ("Remove TradeMark") MUST be in C: and be the FIRST command, otherwise
; the CDTV stays on the splash screen (white logo) and shows nothing.
; =============================================================================
RMTM

Failat 21

; mpmount reads the real geometry from the firmware (TD_GETGEOMETRY) and mounts
; the units present (disk0.hdf..disk3.hdf -> MPD0..MPD3) with the ROM OFS.
; Resizing a .hdf does NOT require rebuilding the CD.
copy DEVS:mpdisk.device RAM:
assign DEVS: RAM:
mpmount
MPD0:C/Assign SYS: MPD0:
MPD0:C/Assign C: MPD0:C
MPD0:C/Assign L: MPD0:L
MPD0:C/Assign LIBS: MPD0:LIBS
MPD0:C/Assign DEVS: MPD0:DEVS
MPD0:C/Assign S: MPD0:S
MPD0:C/Assign FONTS: MPD0:Fonts
MPD0:C/Assign T: RAM:
MPD0:C/execute MPD0:S/Startup-sequence
